{"reason": "The baseline model achieved 0.8328 Recall@10 but plateaued quickly because it discarded direct link graph evidence for 325 out of 355 trackers and utilized an unaligned pointwise loss that ignores top-10 ranking dynamics. Historical experiments show that capturing full link-graph collaborative signals combined with explicit ranking loss functions significantly improves Recall@10. Modifying data processing, model architecture, and training evaluation creates an end-to-end synergy: full 355-tracker link indicators supply definitive physical tracking evidence, an architectural direct bypass preserves this strong evidence into output logits, and a compound ranking loss directly optimizes the top-10 margin.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "model_design", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "Expand direct tracker link extraction from the top 30 to all 355 candidate trackers during the single-pass streaming of link-graph.parquet, mapping matched target domain IDs directly to tracker IDs to form a complete 355-dimensional binary direct-link indicator matrix. Enrich domain lexical representations by upgrading hostname TF-IDF character n-grams from (3, 4) to (2, 5) with TruncatedSVD components increased from 24 to 64, and adding hostname character Shannon entropy, second-level domain length, and subdomain depth counts. Aggregate company-level and category-level tracker link counts using trackers.tsv metadata to capture group-level tracking tendencies. Maintain consistent train/val/test feature matrices (X_train, X_val, X_test) and preserve exact target sparse matrix structures and tracker ID mappings.", "model_design": "Enhance TrackerResNet by incorporating a direct-link residual bypass projection that routes the 355-dimensional direct tracker indicator flags through a linear skip layer straight to the final logits alongside the deep residual representation, preventing high-confidence physical link signals from being smoothed out by deep residual blocks. Formulate a CompoundTop10RankingLoss combining asymmetric binary cross-entropy with a smooth pairwise LogSumExp ranking loss that explicitly penalizes negative tracker logits whenever they outrank true positive tracker logits for each domain. Initialize the direct bypass linear layer with positive diagonal weights to strongly bias directly observed trackers toward the top 10 while allowing deep residual layers to infer unlinked and co-occurring trackers. Preserve the TrackerResNet module interface and ensure model output dimensions remain (batch_size, 355).", "training_evaluation": "Update DataLoader creation and the training loop to feed both the feature matrices and the direct tracker indicator flags into the model and optimize with the CompoundTop10RankingLoss using AdamW with cosine annealing and gradient clipping. Adapt compute_recall_at_10 and test inference routines to supply direct-link flags during batch evaluations, ensuring exact official Recall@10 computation across all validation domains. Maintain the checkpoint saving mechanism based on validation Recall@10, preserve all output file formats (submission.csv and submission.tsv with columns domain_id and tracking_domain_id), and ensure the final validation score is printed exactly as required."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
  "reason": "The baseline model achieved 0.8328 Recall@10 but plateaued quickly because it discarded direct link graph evidence for 325 out of 355 trackers and utilized an unaligned pointwise loss that ignores top-10 ranking dynamics. Historical experiments show that capturing full link-graph collaborative signals combined with explicit ranking loss functions significantly improves Recall@10. Modifying data processing, model architecture, and training evaluation creates an end-to-end synergy: full 355-tracker link indicators supply definitive physical tracking evidence, an architectural direct bypass preserves this strong evidence into output logits, and a compound ranking loss directly optimizes the top-10 margin.",
  "module": [
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering",
    "model_design",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "Expand direct tracker link extraction from the top 30 to all 355 candidate trackers during the single-pass streaming of link-graph.parquet, mapping matched target domain IDs directly to tracker IDs to form a complete 355-dimensional binary direct-link indicator matrix. Enrich domain lexical representations by upgrading hostname TF-IDF character n-grams from (3, 4) to (2, 5) with TruncatedSVD components increased from 24 to 64, and adding hostname character Shannon entropy, second-level domain length, and subdomain depth counts. Aggregate company-level and category-level tracker link counts using trackers.tsv metadata to capture group-level tracking tendencies. Maintain consistent train/val/test feature matrices (X_train, X_val, X_test) and preserve exact target sparse matrix structures and tracker ID mappings.",
    "model_design": "Enhance TrackerResNet by incorporating a direct-link residual bypass projection that routes the 355-dimensional direct tracker indicator flags through a linear skip layer straight to the final logits alongside the deep residual representation, preventing high-confidence physical link signals from being smoothed out by deep residual blocks. Formulate a CompoundTop10RankingLoss combining asymmetric binary cross-entropy with a smooth pairwise LogSumExp ranking loss that explicitly penalizes negative tracker logits whenever they outrank true positive tracker logits for each domain. Initialize the direct bypass linear layer with positive diagonal weights to strongly bias directly observed trackers toward the top 10 while allowing deep residual layers to infer unlinked and co-occurring trackers. Preserve the TrackerResNet module interface and ensure model output dimensions remain (batch_size, 355).",
    "training_evaluation": "Update DataLoader creation and the training loop to feed both the feature matrices and the direct tracker indicator flags into the model and optimize with the CompoundTop10RankingLoss using AdamW with cosine annealing and gradient clipping. Adapt compute_recall_at_10 and test inference routines to supply direct-link flags during batch evaluations, ensuring exact official Recall@10 computation across all validation domains. Maintain the checkpoint saving mechanism based on validation Recall@10, preserve all output file formats (submission.csv and submission.tsv with columns domain_id and tracking_domain_id), and ensure the final validation score is printed exactly as required."
  }
}"}

{"reason": "The baseline achieves 0.8309 Recall@10 but suffers from three primary bottlenecks: graph feature truncation (direct hyperlinks discard tracker identity and collaborative voting is cut off at 35 trackers), gradient dilution (tracker-specific link evidence is compressed through a dense bottleneck), and multi-label ranking misalignment (the fixed 10th-negative loss margin allows true positives to slip beyond rank 10 when domains have multiple trackers). Modifying data_processing_and_feature_engineering, model_design, and training_evaluation addresses these root causes by vectorizing 355-tracker direct link extraction, introducing a dedicated Tracker-Specific Graph Fusion Head with metadata embeddings, and adopting an Adaptive Top-10 Boundary ranking loss strictly aligned with Recall@10.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "model_design", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Expand link-graph feature engineering to capture direct tracker out-links across all 355 trackers and expand collaborative neighbor voting, while augmenting tracker metadata representation. WHY: In the baseline, tracker identities in direct hyperlinks were collapsed into a single scalar counter and voting was truncated to 35 trackers, discarding unambiguous structural signals that directly determine tracker presence. HOW: Construct a lookup table mapping domain IDs to tracker indices (0-354) and accumulate direct tracker hyperlinks using vectorized NumPy bincount across all evaluation domains during parquet streaming, yielding a 355-dimensional direct tracker presence vector alongside degree and neighbor features. Interface constraints: Preserve all existing lexical, SVD, freedom-of-the-press, and URL category features, saving outputs to train_features.parquet, val_features.parquet, test_features.parquet, and feature_metadata.json.", "model_design": "WHAT: Upgrade TrackerAttentionRankNet with a dedicated Tracker-Specific Graph Fusion Head and replace the fixed k=10 hinge penalty with an Adaptive Top-10 Ranking Loss. WHY: Dense MLP bottlenecks dilute high-precision tracker link signals, and comparing positives against only the 10th negative allows false positives to push true trackers into ranks 11+ when domains have multiple ground-truth trackers. HOW: In TrackerAttentionRankNet, add a residual graph fusion stream that projects domain-tracker link features directly into tracker logits, combined with attention-refined tracker metadata embeddings and log-odds prior biases. In the loss function, dynamically set the negative rank threshold per domain to clamp(10 - P_i, min=0, max=9), guaranteeing that clearing the margin places all P_i positive trackers inside the top-10 cutoff. Interface constraints: Maintain model forward signature accepting feature tensor x and returning (batch_size, 355) logits, and keep loss class callable with (logits, targets).", "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Update the training and evaluation loop to train the enhanced TrackerAttentionRankNet with the adaptive ranking loss, handle the expanded feature dimensions, and preserve best-checkpoint evaluation. WHY: Strict synchronization between the data dimensions, adaptive margin ranking loss, learning rate scheduling, and Recall@10 validation is required to ensure consistent convergence and optimal top-10 rankings. HOW: Initialize DataLoader instances with the expanded feature matrices, train for 12 epochs using AdamW with cosine annealing and gradient clipping at 5.0, select the best model checkpoint based on hold-out validation Recall@10, and generate the final predictions in submission/submission.csv and submission.tsv matching target.tsv. Interface constraints: Maintain compute_recall_at_10 metric definition, evaluate function signature, and standard output paths ./submission/submission.csv and ./submission/submission.tsv."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
  "reason": "The baseline achieves 0.8309 Recall@10 but suffers from three primary bottlenecks: graph feature truncation (direct hyperlinks discard tracker identity and collaborative voting is cut off at 35 trackers), gradient dilution (tracker-specific link evidence is compressed through a dense bottleneck), and multi-label ranking misalignment (the fixed 10th-negative loss margin allows true positives to slip beyond rank 10 when domains have multiple trackers). Modifying data_processing_and_feature_engineering, model_design, and training_evaluation addresses these root causes by vectorizing 355-tracker direct link extraction, introducing a dedicated Tracker-Specific Graph Fusion Head with metadata embeddings, and adopting an Adaptive Top-10 Boundary ranking loss strictly aligned with Recall@10.",
  "module": [
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering",
    "model_design",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Expand link-graph feature engineering to capture direct tracker out-links across all 355 trackers and expand collaborative neighbor voting, while augmenting tracker metadata representation. WHY: In the baseline, tracker identities in direct hyperlinks were collapsed into a single scalar counter and voting was truncated to 35 trackers, discarding unambiguous structural signals that directly determine tracker presence. HOW: Construct a lookup table mapping domain IDs to tracker indices (0-354) and accumulate direct tracker hyperlinks using vectorized NumPy bincount across all evaluation domains during parquet streaming, yielding a 355-dimensional direct tracker presence vector alongside degree and neighbor features. Interface constraints: Preserve all existing lexical, SVD, freedom-of-the-press, and URL category features, saving outputs to train_features.parquet, val_features.parquet, test_features.parquet, and feature_metadata.json.",
    "model_design": "WHAT: Upgrade TrackerAttentionRankNet with a dedicated Tracker-Specific Graph Fusion Head and replace the fixed k=10 hinge penalty with an Adaptive Top-10 Ranking Loss. WHY: Dense MLP bottlenecks dilute high-precision tracker link signals, and comparing positives against only the 10th negative allows false positives to push true trackers into ranks 11+ when domains have multiple ground-truth trackers. HOW: In TrackerAttentionRankNet, add a residual graph fusion stream that projects domain-tracker link features directly into tracker logits, combined with attention-refined tracker metadata embeddings and log-odds prior biases. In the loss function, dynamically set the negative rank threshold per domain to clamp(10 - P_i, min=0, max=9), guaranteeing that clearing the margin places all P_i positive trackers inside the top-10 cutoff. Interface constraints: Maintain model forward signature accepting feature tensor x and returning (batch_size, 355) logits, and keep loss class callable with (logits, targets).",
    "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Update the training and evaluation loop to train the enhanced TrackerAttentionRankNet with the adaptive ranking loss, handle the expanded feature dimensions, and preserve best-checkpoint evaluation. WHY: Strict synchronization between the data dimensions, adaptive margin ranking loss, learning rate scheduling, and Recall@10 validation is required to ensure consistent convergence and optimal top-10 rankings. HOW: Initialize DataLoader instances with the expanded feature matrices, train for 12 epochs using AdamW with cosine annealing and gradient clipping at 5.0, select the best model checkpoint based on hold-out validation Recall@10, and generate the final predictions in submission/submission.csv and submission.tsv matching target.tsv. Interface constraints: Maintain compute_recall_at_10 metric definition, evaluate function signature, and standard output paths ./submission/submission.csv and ./submission/submission.tsv."
  }
}"}

{"reason": "Execution finished in only 5 minutes with validation Recall@10 strictly peaking at the final epoch 14 (0.841841), revealing premature training termination. Concurrently, the current model predicts 355 trackers as mutually independent outputs despite tight industrial tracker co-occurrence ecosystems, and the feature representation compresses 5,000 character n-grams into just 64 dimensions while limiting TLDs to 50. Modifying data_processing_and_feature_engineering, model_design, and training_evaluation addresses these root causes by enriching lexical and regional features, introducing empirical label co-occurrence interaction refinement, and expanding training volume and schedule to ensure full convergence.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "model_design", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Expand lexical and geographic features by scaling TruncatedSVD from 64 to 128 components, enlarging the top TLD vocabulary from 50 to 150 with multi-part ccTLD parsing, and expanding binary topical keywords from 12 to 36. WHY: Lexical domain identity is the primary signal for tracker inference when direct hyperlinks are sparse, but 64 SVD components over-smooth hostname representations and 50 TLDs fail to capture high-volume international country codes. HOW: Update get_tld to inspect known two-part ccTLDs (e.g., .co.uk, .com.br, .co.jp), build top-150 TLD one-hot vectors, expand the keyword list to 36 intent terms (such as shop, porn, finance, travel, crypto, betting), and fit TruncatedSVD with n_components=128 on the TF-IDF matrix strictly from training hostnames. Interface constraints: Preserve build_feature_matrix signature, output paths train_features.parquet, val_features.parquet, test_features.parquet, and metadata structure in tracker_metadata.json.", "model_design": "WHAT: Incorporate a trainable empirical Label Interaction Refinement layer into TrackerResNet. WHY: Trackers consistently operate in bundled ecosystems (e.g. Google Analytics with Tag Manager and DoubleClick; Yandex with LiveInternet and Mail.ru), but standard independent classification heads cannot propagate detected presence to conditionally boost correlated partner trackers. HOW: Compute the empirical conditional co-occurrence matrix C where C[j, k] = P(tracker_k | tracker_j) from Y_train with zeroed diagonal, and in TrackerResNet forward pass compute p = sigmoid(logits0), calculate refinement = p @ W_cooccur (with W_cooccur initialized to C * 0.5), and output final_logits = logits0 + refinement. Interface constraints: Preserve TrackerResNet class name, forward signature accepting (x, direct_links), and ensure output shape remains (batch_size, 355).", "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Expand the training sample from 250,000 to 350,000 domains and extend training from 14 to 22 epochs with an aligned CosineAnnealingLR schedule. WHY: The previous run ran in only 5 minutes with validation Recall@10 rising monotonically to 0.841841 at epoch 14 without plateauing, indicating substantial headroom before convergence. HOW: Set N_TRAIN = min(350000, len(shuffled_train_domains) - N_VAL), configure EPOCHS = 22 with T_max = 22 and early stopping patience = 6, maintaining batch size 2048 and AdamW optimizer settings. Interface constraints: Retain compute_recall_at_10 metric evaluation, hold-out validation split size N_VAL=25000, and output file formats to ./submission/submission.csv and ./submission/submission.tsv."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
