    "model_design": "WHAT: Upgrade TrackerAttentionRankNet with a multi-channel tracker graph stream and integrate PPMI spectral embeddings into the tracker metadata self-attention layer. WHY: Direct hyperlink indicators alone are sparse for embedded tracking scripts, and self-attention cannot learn 355x355 cross-tracker interactions from scratch in 12 epochs without prior co-occurrence grounding. HOW: Expand the graph stream into a multi-channel architecture ingesting direct links, in-neighbor distributions, out-neighbor distributions, and log vote counts (4 x 355 features) with a dedicated MLP projection and skip connection, while projecting the 32-dim PPMI embeddings into tracker representations before self-attention refinement, maintaining AdaptiveTop10RankingLoss. Interface constraints: Maintain model forward signature returning (batch_size, 355) logits, and preserve loss class interface callable with (logits, targets).",
    "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Update the training and evaluation pipeline to feed the multi-channel tracker graph features into TrackerAttentionRankNet, train with CosineAnnealingLR, and evaluate Recall@10. WHY: Feature dimensionality expansion and multi-channel graph routing require coordinated tensor extraction in data loaders to ensure seamless training, validation, and test inference. HOW: Track the multi-channel 355-tracker feature index slices from feature_cols, train for 12 epochs using AdamW (lr=1e-3, weight_decay=1e-4) with gradient clipping at 5.0, save best model weights based on validation Recall@10, and generate top-10 candidate predictions. Interface constraints: Preserve compute_recall_at_10, evaluate function signature, and save required submission files to ./submission/submission.csv and ./submission/submission.tsv matching target.tsv formatting."
  }
}"}

{"reason": "Analysis of the current run shows validation loss degrading after epoch 5 from 2.4570 to 2.4988 while Recall@10 plateaued at 0.8399, driven by three root causes: neighbor voting restricted to only 250k domains truncates collaborative graph signals, an unconstrained 1M-parameter dense graph stream causes cross-tracker overfitting, and a single-threshold ranking loss allows high-confidence false positives in ranks 1-9 to escape penalty. Modifying data_processing_and_feature_engineering, model_design, and training_evaluation resolves these bottlenecks by expanding graph voting across the full labeled training pool with enriched tracker metadata, implementing a structured channel-aligned per-tracker projection, and optimizing with a Hard Negative Top-K Margin Ranking Loss.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "model_design", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Expand link-graph neighbor voting to the complete leak-free training pool, enrich tracker metadata with top company and brand one-hot features, and expand hostname character n-gram SVD components from 16 to 32. WHY: Restricting neighbor voting to 250,000 domains discards hundreds of thousands of labeled domains leaving many test domains with sparse votes, while omitting company and brand groupings prevents the model from capturing strong parent ecosystem tracking patterns. HOW: Construct the voting projection matrix against all domains in train_pool to compute normalized in-neighbor and out-neighbor vote distributions across all 355 trackers, extract one-hot encodings for top companies and brands from trackers.tsv to concatenate into tracker_meta_matrix, and fit TruncatedSVD with 32 components on the hostname TF-IDF matrix. Interface constraints: Maintain output parquet filenames (train_features.parquet, val_features.parquet, test_features.parquet) and feature_metadata.json, ensuring domain order matches target.tsv.", "model_design": "WHAT: Replace the monolithic dense graph stream with a structured channel-aligned per-tracker linear projection and upgrade the ranking loss to a Hard Negative Top-K Margin Ranking Loss. WHY: The previous 1420-to-512 dense layer introduced nearly 1 million parameters that learned spurious cross-tracker interactions and overfit by epoch 5, while the single-threshold ranking loss allowed severe false positives in ranks 1 through 9 to escape penalty whenever a true positive beat the single gathered negative. HOW: Reshape the 4 graph feature channels (direct link, in-norm vote, out-norm vote, log vote) to (batch_size, num_trackers, 4) and project with dedicated per-tracker weights plus direct link residual skip into logits; formulate HardNegativeTopKRankingLoss by taking the top-10 hardest negatives for each domain, computing pairwise margin violations against all positive trackers, and combining with asymmetric focal loss. Interface constraints: Preserve the model forward interface accepting tensor x and returning (batch_size, 355) logits, and maintain the loss class callable with (logits, targets).", "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Update training, validation, and inference routines to synchronize with the expanded feature dimensions, channel-aligned tracker projections, and the Hard Negative Top-K Ranking Loss. WHY: Expanding lexical SVD components and replacing the loss function requires cohesive tensor dimension management, scheduler synchronization, and Recall@10 checkpointing to achieve peak ranking performance. HOW: Feed the updated feature matrices into DataLoaders, train TrackerAttentionRankNet for 12 epochs using AdamW (lr=1e-3, weight_decay=1e-4) with CosineAnnealingLR and gradient clipping at 5.0, retain the checkpoint achieving highest validation Recall@10, and generate top-10 tracker predictions mapped to tracking_domain_id. Interface constraints: Preserve compute_recall_at_10 and evaluate function interfaces, producing submission outputs at ./submission/submission.csv and ./submission/submission.tsv matching target.tsv."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
  "reason": "Analysis of the current run shows validation loss degrading after epoch 5 from 2.4570 to 2.4988 while Recall@10 plateaued at 0.8399, driven by three root causes: neighbor voting restricted to only 250k domains truncates collaborative graph signals, an unconstrained 1M-parameter dense graph stream causes cross-tracker overfitting, and a single-threshold ranking loss allows high-confidence false positives in ranks 1-9 to escape penalty. Modifying data_processing_and_feature_engineering, model_design, and training_evaluation resolves these bottlenecks by expanding graph voting across the full labeled training pool with enriched tracker metadata, implementing a structured channel-aligned per-tracker projection, and optimizing with a Hard Negative Top-K Margin Ranking Loss.",
  "module": [
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering",
    "model_design",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Expand link-graph neighbor voting to the complete leak-free training pool, enrich tracker metadata with top company and brand one-hot features, and expand hostname character n-gram SVD components from 16 to 32. WHY: Restricting neighbor voting to 250,000 domains discards hundreds of thousands of labeled domains leaving many test domains with sparse votes, while omitting company and brand groupings prevents the model from capturing strong parent ecosystem tracking patterns. HOW: Construct the voting projection matrix against all domains in train_pool to compute normalized in-neighbor and out-neighbor vote distributions across all 355 trackers, extract one-hot encodings for top companies and brands from trackers.tsv to concatenate into tracker_meta_matrix, and fit TruncatedSVD with 32 components on the hostname TF-IDF matrix. Interface constraints: Maintain output parquet filenames (train_features.parquet, val_features.parquet, test_features.parquet) and feature_metadata.json, ensuring domain order matches target.tsv.",
    "model_design": "WHAT: Replace the monolithic dense graph stream with a structured channel-aligned per-tracker linear projection and upgrade the ranking loss to a Hard Negative Top-K Margin Ranking Loss. WHY: The previous 1420-to-512 dense layer introduced nearly 1 million parameters that learned spurious cross-tracker interactions and overfit by epoch 5, while the single-threshold ranking loss allowed severe false positives in ranks 1 through 9 to escape penalty whenever a true positive beat the single gathered negative. HOW: Reshape the 4 graph feature channels (direct link, in-norm vote, out-norm vote, log vote) to (batch_size, num_trackers, 4) and project with dedicated per-tracker weights plus direct link residual skip into logits; formulate HardNegativeTopKRankingLoss by taking the top-10 hardest negatives for each domain, computing pairwise margin violations against all positive trackers, and combining with asymmetric focal loss. Interface constraints: Preserve the model forward interface accepting tensor x and returning (batch_size, 355) logits, and maintain the loss class callable with (logits, targets).",
    "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Update training, validation, and inference routines to synchronize with the expanded feature dimensions, channel-aligned tracker projections, and the Hard Negative Top-K Ranking Loss. WHY: Expanding lexical SVD components and replacing the loss function requires cohesive tensor dimension management, scheduler synchronization, and Recall@10 checkpointing to achieve peak ranking performance. HOW: Feed the updated feature matrices into DataLoaders, train TrackerAttentionRankNet for 12 epochs using AdamW (lr=1e-3, weight_decay=1e-4) with CosineAnnealingLR and gradient clipping at 5.0, retain the checkpoint achieving highest validation Recall@10, and generate top-10 tracker predictions mapped to tracking_domain_id. Interface constraints: Preserve compute_recall_at_10 and evaluate function interfaces, producing submission outputs at ./submission/submission.csv and ./submission/submission.tsv matching target.tsv."
